WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.940
Welcome to the Singularity Daily, Monday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.300
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in superintelligence.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.900
Give it away.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.720
Anthropic's seven co-founders say they'll donate 80% of their shares.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.250
That's about $112 billion, and charities are gearing up.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.030
This week, Mira Murati's Thinking Machines released a free model,

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.530
Inkling 2 Mini, that runs on a laptop.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.700
A startup says its AI agents designed a new chip from scratch,

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.370
4.5 times as efficient.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.990
But in a pretend software office,

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.830
even top coding agents finished fewer than one task in ten.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:58.140
In China, Tencent let outside safety testers check its new model.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.950
Hacking skills? Limited.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.930
Now, the money.

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:05.150
Elon Musk warns that next year's cash shortage is going to be nuts.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.870
SpaceX is borrowing $43 billion for Nvidia chips,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:14.520
and its lenders don't want them launched into space.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.790
UBS sees AI investment hitting $1.4 trillion next year. The returns? Uncertain.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.020
And Google's giving Sundar Pichai's old college,

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:29.170
IIT Kharagpur, $5 million for AI research.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.150
In a new study, people who quit AI chatbots for two weeks felt a bit less lonely,

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:36.490
and socialised more.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.020
Meanwhile, a Guardian columnist answered her husband's texts with her phone's AI replies.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.140
He didn't notice.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.330
The catch? South Korea's education minister quit,

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.870
after rushed rules on AI cheating caused confusion.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:55.190
In London, hundreds marched for an AI pause.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.630
In Lithuania, a robot called ALTAS joins a library's staff in the New Year,

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:07.960
to get kids reading.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.980
In France, a towel-folding robot gets the job right 99.5% of the time.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.520
And an OpenAI patent filing describes ea

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:20.100
rbuds that read the words you only mouth.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.910
Give away the money, give away the code,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.610
and once in a while, give the chatbot a rest.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.670
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.930
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.230
That's the Singularity Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.340
Go build something. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
